abstract: >
  The Acoustic Habitability Erosion Index (IEH-A) is a research instrument that
  measures the contraction of an inhabitant's practical world under sustained
  urban-noise exposure — a dimension not captured by clinical noise scales or
  soundscape descriptors. This repository opens the instrument as a common
  protocol for a distributed, multi-context validation consortium.
keywords:
  - urban soundscape
  - acoustic habitability
  - urban noise
  - measurement invariance
  - distributed validation
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >
      Índice de Erosión del Habitar Acústico (IEH-A): instrumento para el
      diagnóstico diferencial de la exposición a ruido urbano
